wo passes. GPT-6.1 Sol was ahead by +4.8 after move 12 and had a +8.1 lead after the 20k's H7, but a run of costly moves in the middle game gave it all back. The 20k lost 22.4 points with H5 at move 26 and still won, because GPT-6.1 Sol's own losses were larger and more frequent: 9 blunders against 6, and a mean of 3.8 points lost per move against 3.3.", "moments": [{"turn": 13, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's B7 took Black from +4.8 to -6.2, an 11.0-point loss. The engine wanted D7, the point Black only played at move 17. The lead reversed here for the first time."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "With Black at +8.1 and a wall along the seventh line, F7 lost 14.2 points and dropped Black to -6.1. The engine's choice was G2. This is where the lead from the earlier fights slipped away."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "The 20k's H5 lost 22.4 points, the worst move of the game, and swung the lead from -19.5 to +2.9. It was a reprieve that White needed, because Black's H8 had just lost 16.3 points."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "D3 lost 17.1 points and sent Black from +2.9 to -14.2. It was the worst move of GPT-6.1 Sol's game. The engine's choice was F2, which it preferred at almost every turn through the middle of the game."}, {"turn": 44, "text": "White's A6 took the lead from -8.3 to +4.1. GPT-6.1 Sol's H2 on the previous turn had lost 6.2 points, and A6 returned the favour. The 20k took a 12.4-point swing and GPT-6.1 Sol never got back into the game."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran (game-047-inspection.js, game-047-verification.js, the file reads and patch writes) parses the returned board, computes groups, liberties and empty regions of the current position, logs records, replays the actual move history to check boards and captures, and counts final area. None of it loops over candidate moves, scores or ranks them, or plays out hypothetical continuations; the move choices and the tactical lines in the notes were written by hand.", "stop": false}